<title>ITALY: BCI group buys Seat stake for 1.58 trln lire.</title>
<headline>BCI group buys Seat stake for 1.58 trln lire.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Banca Commerciale Italiana (BCI) bought a stake in telephone directory publisher Seat for 1.58 trillion lire, the Treasury said.</p>
<p>The Treasury said in a statement that the purchase valued Seat, which was spun off from Italian telecommunications giant Stet earlier this year, at 3.20 trillion lire.</p>
<p>The BCI group outpriced one other final bidder, ITT World Directories, to win the 61.7 percent stake the Treasury holds in Seat, it said.</p>
<p>Another initial contender, GTE Directories, part of U.S. group GTE Corp, pulled out of final bidding.</p>
<p>-- Rome Newsroom +39 6 678 2501</p>
</text>
